    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37219" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξετ-αστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>capable of examining into,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἔργων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					1.1.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καὶ κριτικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Herm.</u>
					64
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πρὸς ἀκρίβειαν</span>”
				<i>exacting,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					7p.429M.
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>fitted for inquiry,</i> of Dialectic, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Top.</u>
				101b3
			</span></i> (in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Po.</u>
				1455a34
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκστατικοί</span> is prob. l.). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					17.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργύριον</span>), τό, <i>salary
				of an</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξεταστής,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				13.4
			</span></i>.</div>
